// `xs[0]` on a `list<int>` is the instruction the build already emits for
// `xs.get(0)`: `compiler/ir/builder.orb` lowers both spellings to
// `IROpcode.list_get`, and this pass prints that one as `call <type> get`. The
// element kind is the one the source wrote in the receiver's type text, so the
// index form answers `int` where it used to be a give-up.
//
// A list written without an element kind stays a give-up. `list` alone says
// nothing about the inside, and an invented element type is the lie the
// `unknown` count exists to make visible. Emitting the instruction anyway would
// add an `unknown` while suppressing the same file text.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "fn first(xs: list<int>) -> int { return xs[0] }"
    print(compileFrontendSource("fixture", source))
}
